      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Example: Multilevel Inheritance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In multilevel inheritance, class B inherits from class A and class C inherits from class B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how the inheritance looks like:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Class C inherits form Class B which inherits from Class A which is Multilevel inheritance",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Source Code"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "1class A {\n2    public void methodA() {\n3        System.out.println(\"Method of class A\");\n4    }\n5}\n6\n7class B extends A {\n8    public void methodB() {\n9        System.out.println(\"Method of class B\");\n10    }\n11}\n12\n13class C extends B {\n14    \n15}\n16\n17class Main {\n18    public static void main(String[] args) {\n19        \n20        // object of class C\n21        C obj = new C();\n22        \n23        // call method of class B\n24        obj.methodB();\n25        \n26        // call method of class A\n27        obj.methodA();\n28    }\n29}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Method of class B\nMethod of class A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, when class B inherits class A, the method of class A is now inherited to B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "That's why object of class C is able to access methods of both classes A and B, even though it only inherits class B."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
